DTSTAMP:20261023T000000Z
DTSTART:20261023T031500
DTEND:20261023T051500
SUMMARY:Orionid Meteor Shower: Halley's Comet dust
DESCRIPTION:These are crumbs off Halley's Comet hitting the air at forty-o
 ne miles a second. The catch this year is a fat gibbous moon that washes 
 the sky out until it sets at quarter past three\, which leaves about two 
 and a half hours of real darkness before dawn on the 22nd.\nPrice: Free\n
 Area: Pensacola Beach & Perdido\nTimes: Thu 10/22/2026 · from 3:15 AM\, 
 once the moon is down\nChecked against the venue's own page on 2026-10-02
 \nhttps://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-orionids-1022.html
LOCATION:Your own yard\, or Big Lagoon State Park for a darker sky\, 12301
  Gulf Beach Hwy\, Pensacola\, FL 32507
URL:https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-orionids-1022.html
END:VEVENT
